{
  "an3.36:0.1": "Numbered Discourses 3.36 ",
  "an3.36:0.2": "4. Messengers of the Gods ",
  "an3.36:0.3": "Messengers of the Gods ",
  "an3.36:1.1": "“There are, mendicants, these three messengers of the gods. ",
  "an3.36:1.2": "What three? ",
  "an3.36:1.3": "Firstly, someone does bad things by way of body, speech, and mind. ",
  "an3.36:1.4": "When their body breaks up, after death, they’re reborn in a place of loss, a bad place, the underworld, hell. ",
  "an3.36:1.5": "The wardens of hell take them by the arms and present them to King Yama, saying, ",
  "an3.36:1.6": "‘Your Majesty, this person did not pay due respect to their mother and father, ascetics and brahmins, or honor the elders in the family. ",
  "an3.36:1.7": "May Your Majesty punish them!’ ",
  "an3.36:2.1": "King Yama pursues, presses, and grills them about the first messenger of the gods: ",
  "an3.36:2.2": "‘My man, did you not see the first messenger of the gods that appeared among human beings?’ ",
  "an3.36:2.3": "They say, ",
  "an3.36:2.4": "‘I saw nothing, sir.’ ",
  "an3.36:3.1": "King Yama says to them, ",
  "an3.36:3.2": "‘My man, did you not see among human beings an elderly woman or a man—eighty, ninety, or a hundred years old—bent double, crooked, leaning on a staff, trembling as they walk, ailing, past their prime, with teeth broken, hair grey and scanty or bald, skin wrinkled, and limbs blotchy?’ ",
  "an3.36:3.3": "They say, ",
  "an3.36:3.4": "‘I saw that, sir.’ ",
  "an3.36:4.1": "King Yama sa